        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Switch Type"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "generation": "1770735919466",
            "regeneration": "1770736085797"
          },
          "code": "SWITCH_TYPE",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1770735166769",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770735166770_1",
              "name": "caseExpression",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.type}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SWITCH"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Posting Description Generation"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "POSTING_DESCRIPTION_GENERATION",
          "id": "1770735919466",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770735919467_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## instructions\nYour task is to write a job posting for the role of {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.requisitionTitle}} for the company {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.companyName}} in the {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.divisionName}} department.\nUse the additional information provided by the user to generate the job description. ## user_provided_information {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \n\nUse the following rules in generating the response.\n              1. The job posting should include multiple sections: summary, description, responsibilities, qualifications.\n              2. The summary should be no more than 50 words.\n              3. Limit the responsibilities to no more than 10 items.\n              4. Limit the qualifications to no more than 10 items.\n              5. Format the response as an RFC8259 compliant JSON object in the following format:\n              {\n                  \"summary\": \"<insert a short summary of the job position>\",\n                  \"description\": \"<insert a medium paragraph to describe the job position>\",\n                  \"responsibilities\": [\n                      <strictly no more than 10 items in this array>\n                  ],\n                  \"qualifications\":  [\n                      <strictly no more than 10 items in this array>\n                  ]\n              }"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Posting Description Regeneration"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "POSTING_DESCRIPTION_REGENERATION",
          "id": "1770736085797",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770736085798_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## instructions\nYour task is to write a job posting for the role of {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.requisitionTitle}} for the company {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.companyName}} in the {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.divisionName}} department.\nUse the additional information provided by the user to generate the job description. ## user_provided_information {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nKeep the current job posting description in context while regenerating and improvise on that.\nCurrent Job Posting Description: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.currentJobPostingDescription}} \n\nUse the following rules in generating the response.\n              1. The job posting should include multiple sections: summary, description, responsibilities, qualifications.\n              2. The summary should be no more than 50 words.\n              3. Limit the responsibilities to no more than 10 items.\n              4. Limit the qualifications to no more than 10 items.\n              5. Format the response as an RFC8259 compliant JSON object in the following format:\n              {\n                  \"summary\": \"<insert a short summary of the job position>\",\n                  \"description\": \"<insert a medium paragraph to describe the job position>\",\n                  \"responsibilities\": [\n                      <strictly no more than 10 items in this array>\n                  ],\n                  \"qualifications\":  [\n                      <strictly no more than 10 items in this array>\n                  ]\n              }"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
      "rootNode": "start",
